/E (We used ResNet101 to evaluate whether increasing the network depth to 101 layers could lead to better performance in our crowd counting model. ResNet is specifically designed to overcome the vanishing gradient problem through the use of residual connections, which allow the network to maintain effective learning even as it becomes deeper. Once ResNet101 completes the feature extraction, we introduced a decoder using Conv2DTranspose layers and upsampling to restore the spatial resolution, ensuring that the output size closely matches the input image.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
